ACCESS CONTROL POLICY - Version 1.0

This policy establishes access control requirements for least privilege, separation of duties, and non-privileged account usage.

1. LEAST PRIVILEGE
   Users shall be granted only the minimum access rights required to perform their job functions.
   Access rights shall be reviewed quarterly and revoked upon role change or termination.

2. SEPARATION OF DUTIES
   Critical functions shall be divided among multiple users to prevent fraud and error.
   No single user shall have the ability to execute a complete sensitive transaction without oversight.

3. NON-PRIVILEGED ACCOUNTS
   Privileged accounts (admin, root) shall only be used when elevated privileges are required.
   Day-to-day activities shall be performed using standard user accounts.
   All privileged access shall be logged and audited.

4. ACCOUNT MANAGEMENT
   Account creation, modification, and deletion require manager approval.
   Shared accounts are prohibited except for documented system accounts.
   Passwords must meet complexity requirements: 12+ characters, mixed case, numbers, and symbols.

5. REMOTE ACCESS
   Remote access requires multi-factor authentication (MFA).
   VPN connections are encrypted using AES-256.
   Remote sessions are terminated after 30 minutes of inactivity.

Effective Date: 2025-01-01
Owner: Information Security Team
Review Cycle: Annual
